			<div class="content" id="post-content-1643664">
									

<p>You know, I kind of like the idea. What really kills this for me is the writing<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-469532-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-469532-1')">1</a></sup>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Lots of informal quotations in place of a clinical explanation of what it does.
<ul>
<li>One subject described rotating SCP-1430 as “like swinging a baseball bat underwater”.</li>
<li>to roughly the intensity “of a dim flashlight”</li>
<li>though with a stilted, “unpracticed” or “unnatural” voice</li>
<li>but instead attempts to “speak”</li>
<li>Subject occasionally coughs mid “word” to spit up blood.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Some difficulties with sentence structure.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-469532-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-469532-2')">2</a></sup>
<ul>
<li>Adorning the top is the seal of the University of ████████, the original location of the object's retrieval, the figure of a adult male breaking away from chains, presumably the “bonds of ignorance” described in an associated recovered document, as well as a woman holding a [REDACTED] emits faint visible light when in low light conditions, or exposed to certain chelating agents.</li>
<li>However, after three hours and forty seven minutes, subject’s narrative takes an unexpected turn, no longer instructing listeners to seek guidance, but instead insisting on self-mutilation, or other violent punishments for increasingly mundane “sins”, differing greatly from standard Methodist doctrine.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Unnecessary sentences that clutter up the piece from a literary standpoint. Less is more.
<ul>
<li>The entire second paragraph.</li>
<li>The light at the tip of it. Blatant literary device, no obvious point from an in-universe standpoint.</li>
<li>Chosen topics of speech have included abstract mathematics, molecular biology, “jerry-rigging”, military tactics, the construction and use of shanks, religious studies, and “gettin’ them █████ ███ ████”. This effect extends to subjects who would normally not choose to speak publicly, including self described introverts, and after sufficient exposure even psychologically traumatized subjects who, under normal circumstances would be effectively mute, will speak (though with a stilted, “unpracticed” or “unnatural” voice).<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-469532-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-469532-3')">3</a></sup></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Bad formatting that, to an experienced reader, is grating. We have a template on the <a href="/how-to-write-an-scp">How to Write an SCP</a> page, and plenty of articles to look to for examples.
<ul>
<li><strong>Object #:</strong></li>
<li><strong>Special containment procedures:</strong></li>
<li><strong>Object Description:</strong></li>
<li>No spacing in the collapsed logs.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Misuse of 'however'. Incorrect: &quot;X, however Y&quot;. Correct: &quot;X; however, Y&quot;. That always grinds my goat.</li>
</ul>
<p>And, uh, are those boxes blacking out &quot;bitch ass hoes&quot;? :I</p>
<p>Anyways, -1. I'm not entirely sure what to think, because although you did a lot (really, a <em>lot</em>) of things wrong that would normally point to sloppy writing and low effort, your attention to detail at some points was refreshing, and clearly you have lots of imagination and put lots of work into this. Keep practicing, I'm sure we'll get something good out of you some day.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-469532-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-469532-1')">1</a>. This is not a comprehensive list.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-469532-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-469532-2')">2</a>. Each sentence gets one idea, and one paragraph gets a related set of ideas. Each sentence has to flow logically to the next, and the paragraphs should be arranged to form the most logical structure for the piece.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-469532-3"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-469532-3')">3</a>. You could simply cut these lines and change &quot;held by a subject&quot; to &quot;held by any subject&quot; and remove whole sentences that add nothing to your piece.</div>
</div>

